{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SVNvwdHucGiASbenUddoTk","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-i3aa4cen\ntotal 8\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff     128 Oct  2 16:34 .\ndrwx------@ 13047 brenn  staff  417504 Oct  2 16:34 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    13 brenn  staff     416 Oct  2 12:20 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff    3888 Oct  2 16:34 sheet.md\n# Gap hunt: A05 — Operational lookup\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for A05:** Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## A05.1\n\n**Check:** Each audit record carries the agent-type-id and agent-instance-id, which resolve to a stored deployment manifest and a live instance.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check `agent.type.id` and `agent.instance.id` are written on every record. 3) Check the type ID can be looked up to a stored manifest (registry, manifest store, file keyed by hash). 4) Answer no if either field is missing or nothing stores manifests by that ID. Answer unknown if the lookup store is outside this repo.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Manifest store, on-call mapping and per-instance containment are not shown in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## A05.2\n\n**Check:** An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Look for CODEOWNERS, `catalog-info.yaml`, `.brace/deployment.yaml`, or another ownership file. 2) Check each agent type maps to a team and to a current operator or on-call rotation. 3) Answer no if an agent type has no owner, or owners exist only in prose with no link. Answer unknown if ownership lives in an outside catalog.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Manifest store, on-call mapping and per-instance containment are not shown in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## A05.3\n\n**Check:** A containment control can disable a single instance or a single agent type (for example revoke its principal or scale it to zero) without touching the launching user's credentials.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find stop and revoke controls: admin endpoints, CLIs, feature flags, scale-to-zero, per-instance token revocation. 2) Check their scope is one instance or one agent type. 3) Answer no if the only control is a global switch or revoking a shared or user credential. Answer unknown if containment is run by an outside platform.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Manifest store, on-call mapping and per-instance containment are not shown in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to A05.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"A05\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"A05.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is